From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 17:13:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: cubie-a7s: Allow eMMC modules in
 the SD slot

Radxa offers an eMMC-to-microSD adapter for the board's microSD slot,
and the boot ROM and U-Boot boot from an eMMC module on it. Linux does
not, because the slot is marked no-mmc, so a system on the module
cannot find its root.

Drop no-mmc. With the A733 SD controllers no longer offering DDR52, such
a module runs at High Speed SDR, 52 MHz, 4 bit, as in the boot loader.
SD cards are not affected: the core tries SD before MMC.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: the SD slot no longer excludes MMC cards and
an SD card still attaches at SDR104; an eMMC module on a microSD
adapter was not at hand.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
index 80f65c643263..6b3967b05a67 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
@@ -393,7 +393,6 @@ &mmc0 {
 	vmmc-supply = <&reg_swout2>;
 	cd-gpios = <&pio 5 6 (GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH | GPIO_PULL_DOWN)>; /* PF6 */
 	bus-width = <4>;
-	no-mmc;
 	no-sdio;
 	sd-uhs-sdr50;
 	sd-uhs-sdr104;
